1 NAME Martim /da Boemia/ II
2 GIVN Martim
2 NSFX II
2 _MARNM da Boemia
2 NICK Martin Behaim
2 NICK Martin von Behaim
2 NICK Martinho da Boémia
2 NICK Martin Bohemus
2 NICK Martin Behaim von Schwarzbach
2 NICK Martinus de Boemia
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 6 OCT 1459
2 ADDR
3 CITY Nuremberg
3 STAE Bavaria
3 CTRY Germany
1 BURI
2 DATE 29 JUL 1507
2 PLAC São Domingo
2 ADDR
3 CITY Lisbon
3 STAE Lisboa
3 CTRY Portugal
1 DEAT
2 DATE 29 JUL 1507
2 ADDR
3 CITY Lisbon
3 CTRY Portugal
1 OCCU Merchant and Explorer
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Martin Behaim (1459 – 1507) was a German mariner, artist, cosmographer, astronomer, philosopher, geographer and explorer in service to [http://www.geni.com/people/Jo%C3%A3o-II-o-Pr%C3%ADncipe-Perfeito-rei-de-Portug
2 CONC al/6000000000350865266/ '''King John II of Portugal'''] (1).
2 CONT
2 CONT 1459: Born in Nürnberg.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1476 (age 17): Travels to Mecheln and Antwerp as merchant for the Nürnberger Hirschvogel family.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1484 (age 25): Travels to Lisbon and constructs the navigational instrument termed the ''Jacob's Rod''.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1485 (age 26): Knighted by King John II of Portugal.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1485 - 1486: Accompanies the Portuguese explorer Diogo Cam (Cão) on a his 2nd expedition to the coast of West Africa and is part of the team that discoveres the mouth of the Congo River.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1486 (age 27): Marries Joana de Macedo in Horta, Azores.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1489 (age 30): Birth of his son Martin.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1491 (age 32): Returns to Nürnberg and finalizes construction of the first globe of the world (the ''Erdapfel'').
2 CONT
2 CONT 1493 (age 34): Returns to Horta.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1507 (age 47): Dies on a travel to Lisbon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Martin Behaim was acclaimed as the actual discoverer of America in the famous Nürnberger chronicle published by [http://www.geni.com/people/Anton-Koberger/6000000014885235568/ '''Anton Koberger''] in Nürnberg 12th July 1493 - only
2 CONC  four months after the return of [http://www.geni.com/people/Jo%C3%A3o-II-o-Pr%C3%ADncipe-Perfeito-rei-de-Portugal/6000000000350865266/ '''Christopher Columbus'''].
2 CONT
2 CONT Stated on leaf CCXC in Koberger (1493): ''The King of Portugal, Juan II. (4), sent, in 1483, James Canus, a native of Portugal, and Martin Behaim of Nuremberg, with some galleys to Ethiopia; that they sent to the Southern Sea, and
2 CONC  near the coast, and, after crossing the line, reached the New World, where, when they happened to look towards the East, their shadow, at noon, appeared on the right; that in that region they discovered lands, heretofore unknown,
2 CONC  which had not been searched after by any people for many years, except the Genoese, and that in vain; finally, that after a navigation of twenty-six months they returned to Portugal; and in proof of their discovery brought pepper
2 CONC  and grana paradisi.''
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) http://www.deutsche-biographie.de/sfz3529.html, http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martin_Behaim and http://www.zeit.de/2007/31/A-Behaim
