1 NAME Philippine /Welser/
2 GIVN Philippine
2 SURN Welser
2 _MARNM von Österreich
2 NICK Filipina
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1 JAN 1527
2 ADDR
3 CITY Augsburg
3 STAE Bavaria (Bayern)
3 CTRY Holy Roman Empire
1 DEAT
2 DATE 24 APR 1580
2 PLAC Schloss Ambras
2 ADDR
3 CITY Innsbruck
3 STAE Duchy of Austria
3 CTRY Holy Roman Empire
1 OCCU Freiin von Zinnenburg, Fürstin von Ambrass und Hohenberg
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Philippine Welser (1527 – 24 April 1580) was the morganatic wife of Ferdinand II, Archduke of Austria. She was granted the titles Baroness of Zinnenburg, Margravine of Burgau, Landgravine of Mellenburg and Countess
2 CONC  of Oberhohenberg and Niederhohenberg.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born in Augsburg. Her family, the Welsers of Augsburg, were merchants and financiers of European significance and great wealth. Her father was Franz (Friedrich) Welser (1497-1572) and her mother was Anna Adler (1507-1572).
2 CONC  Philippine Welser's uncle Bartholomeus V. Welser received Venezuela as security for a loan from the King of Spain in 1528, and the family thus became rulers of the colony. Already at a young age, she was renowned for both her bea
2 CONC uty and her learning. She died at Schloss Ambras, Innsbruck in Tyrol.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the mother of Margrave Andrew of Burgau, who became a Cardinal, and Charles, Margrave of Burgau, who became a noted General. After her death, her husband remarried to Anne Juliana Gonzaga and became the father of Anna of T
2 CONC yrol, who would become Holy Roman Empress.
2 CONT
2 CONT FYI:
2 CONT
2 CONT Morganatic marriage, sometimes called a left-handed marriage,[1] is a marriage between people of unequal social rank, which in the context of royalty prevents the passage of the husband's titles and privileges to the wife and any 
2 CONC children born of the marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Generally, this is a marriage between a man of high birth (such as from a reigning, deposed or mediatised dynasty) and a woman of lesser status (such as a daughter of a low-ranked noble family or a commoner).[2][3] Usually, neithe
2 CONC r the bride nor any children of the marriage have a claim on the bridegroom's succession rights, titles, precedence, or entailed property. The children are considered legitimate for all other purposes and the prohibition against b
2 CONC igamy applies.[3][4] In some countries, a woman could also marry a man of lower rank morganatically
2 CONT
2 CONT Added by Janet Milburn 9/28/2019
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippine Welser, Freiin von Zinnenburg is my/our 7th cousin 13 times removed. ________________________________
