1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hun vokste opp hos formynder: Peder Richardsen Hagerup og hustru Elisabet Sofie Johannesdatter Irgens. Peder Richardsen var bror til hennes biologiske mor Anne Richardsdatter Hagerup.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Death record for Madame Irgens at Stod, Nord Trondelag 27 Sep 1757 gives age at death: 86 years (b. ca. 1871). http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:kb_read?urnread_imagesize=gigant&info=ingen&hode=nei&show=84&uid=482371&js=j
2 CONT
2 CONT [Source of following notes: from Hagerup Family Tree http://genealogy.hagerup.com/ 
2 CONT
2 CONT FamilySearch - Interntional Genealogical Index IGI record Christening: Copy write: Intellectual reserve INC
2 CONT
2 CONT AFN M5P3-P6
2 CONT
2 CONT LDS church submitter: Kaare Bye
2 CONT
2 CONT She is probably not a biological daugther of Peter Richertsen Hagerup, as he is described as her guardian in a division of inheritance in 1693 after her "father". There might however be 2 "Helle" Hagerup at the time. This indivuda
2 CONC l is mentioned as Helle Henriksdatter and her father might be Henrik "NN", Source: Contact: Gary E. Hansen Sr. gahansen2@junoc9T.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Another . . .(possible) solution is that she is the daugther of Henrich Sigismund Hassius HAGERUP b. 1630 and living in Kongberg and working with the silver mines in that city. He married one of the Irgens daugthers. . . . 
2 CONT
2 CONT  . . . En LDS kilde hvder at hun var født på Fossum, Stod, Steinkjer, Nord-Trøndelag. Stod ligger v/ E6 på vei nordover.
2 CONT
2 CONT Foreldrene døde før jentene var (helt) voksne og de vokste opp på Rorøs og er omtalt i arveskifte der.]
2 CONT
2 CONT [Source:Ancestry.com Hansen Kurpierz Rozmus Snopek Genealogy Updated: 2005-12-28 18:15:02 UTC (Wed) Contact: Gary E. Hansen, Sr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Henrich Richertsen Hagerup a brother of Peder Richertsen Hagerup. Henrich presumably was a sailor who died at a young age. It is assumed that due to her father's death, Helle came to live with her uncle Peder Hagerup a
2 CONC nd his wife, Elisabeth Sophie Irgens and later with Elisabeth's brother, Bostrup Irgens. Bostrup and Elisabeth were siblings of Helle's husband Johannes' father, Henning Irgens. This possibly caused the error of Helle's listing as
2 CONC  Elisabeth and Peder's daughter in Slegten Irgens. Helle died at Fossum in Stod Sep 27, 1757 at the home of her son-in-law, Judge Rosted. In 1740 she is mentioned as a widow when she applied for a price increase for her charcoal d
2 CONC elivered to Dragaas Smelting Works.]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
