1 TITL Dr. med.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Ambrosius Jung''', Senior or I (1471–1548) '''was a German humanist, physician, doctor of medical sciences, university professor, and expert in epidemiological diseases'''. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was the physician''' (or one of them) '''for the Emperor Maximilian I''' (1459–1519). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ambrosius Jung was son of Johann Hans Jung (1425–1505) and his wife Anna Imhof (1440–1458), and father of Ambrosius Jung II (1510–1559).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He studied with one of his brothers in Tübingen, and also graduated from the medical faculty in Padua (Padova), where he received his doctorate'''. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From his early youth he collected books and had a large library, which later partly enriched the city's collections (including the medical works of the Jungs). The development of the library was made possible by the acquaintance o
2 CONC f https://www.geni.com/people/Konrad-Peutinger/6000000035172417204, who dedicated one of his controversial works to Ambrosius Jung.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jung also devoted himself to research on the plague'''. He announced the results of his research in 1535, publishing: "A useful, comforting and brief instruction on how to stand firm in the face of the terrible plague ... in or
2 CONC der to help and help the common man who has helped others". In this work, he recommended special precautions to avoid epidemics (including personal hygiene, fumigation and smoking).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ambrosius Jung, according to medical historian Gundolf Keil (b. 1934), was a great expert and authority on epidemiological diseases in 16th-century Europe, a recognized and respected figure in the scientific community of that t
2 CONC ime'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT *
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Works''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Ein ausserwelt loblich tractat und regiment in dem schwärzen zeit der pestilentz (1494) 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Tractatus de pestilentia ex diversis auctoribus aggregatus (1494) 
2 CONT
2 CONT * De morbo mal de Franco (1498, together with his father Johann Hans Jung) 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Ain nutzliche trostliche und kurtze underrichtung, wie man sich in disen schwären leüffen der Pestilentz halte(n) soll ... dem gemainen mann zu hilff und gutem, der mit andern beystand hat, verordnet (1535) 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Remedia manuscripta pro catarrho et angustiis thoracis 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Conchisiones et propositiones universarum medicinam per genera com prehendentes (1538, razem z bratem Ulrichem Jungiem)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT *
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliography
2 CONT
2 CONT * Enzyklopädie Medizingeschichte (ed. Werner Gerabek, Bernhard D. Haage, Gundolf Keil, Wolfgang Wegner, 2005, pp. 709–710, ISBN  3-11-015714-4 )
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reinhard Wolfgang Augsburger Eliten des 16. Jahrhunderts, Akademie Verlag, Augsburg 1995
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Prof. Dr. Gundolf Keil
2 CONT https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gundolf_Keil
2 CONT
