1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Augustin Cranach (* 1554 in Wittenberg , † July 26, 1595 ibid) was a German painter.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Lucas Cranach the Younger and Magdalena Schurff. On March 6, 1564, he enrolled at the University of Wittenberg . Augustin Cranach continued the tradition of the Cranach workshop and held several honorable posts. 
2 CONC On November 26, 1577 he married Marie Selfisch (born January 27, 1558 in Wittenberg, † January 15, 1626 in Delitzsch), a daughter of the Wittenberg bookseller and mayor Samuel Selfisch .
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1584 and 1587 he became a council member in Wittenberg and was also a member of the council in 1590 as councilor and in 1593 as a city judge. In addition to Conrad Fluth, Augustin Cranach was a deputy to bring Polykarp Leyser t
2 CONC he Elder from Braunschweig back to Wittenberg as General Superintendent.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on July 26, 1595 in Wittenberg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendants  His children born in Wittenberg were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Magdalena (born March 17, 1579 in Wittenberg, † November 13, 1617 in Dresden), married on January 25, 1597 with Leonhard Cöppel from Nuremberg († 1637)
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth (born January 8, 1581, † December 14, 1581)
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara (born September 30, 1582, † September 25, 1586)
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Maria (born August 2, 1584, † January 2, 1585 in Wittenberg)
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucas Cranach III. (* March 6, 1586; † before September 15, 1645 in Wittenberg)
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel (born May 12, 1588)
2 CONT
2 CONT Euphrosina (born November 6, 1590, † March 25, 1665) was married to Aegidius Strauch on January 20, 1607 .
2 CONT
2 CONT Augustus (born October 10, 1592)
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Christoph (born January 8, 1594), married with Maria Schuffer
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth (born December 16, 1595), married with Siegfried Neuhofen
2 CONT
2 CONT https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Augustin_Cranach
